msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is our pleasure to announce the release of Quarkus 2.15.0.Final, the last "
"minor release of 2022."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As usual, it comes with bugfixes and small enhancements all over the place "
"together with more important changes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for AWS Lambda SnapStart"
msgstr ""

msgid "Move gRPC extension to new Vert.x gRPC implementation"
msgstr ""

msgid "Federation support for SmallRye GraphQL"
msgstr ""

msgid "Redis - Implement the search group"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add `@ClientQueryParam` to Reactive REST Client"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support filtering by named queries in REST Data with Panache extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for OIDC FrontChannel logout"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM - IN clause parameter padding"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support continuous testing in CLI test command"
msgstr ""

msgid "Introduce image build / push commands"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use -XX:ArchiveClassesAtExit for AppCDS creation in Java 17+"
msgstr ""

msgid "Add Dev Services for Kubernetes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Google Cloud Functions test framework"
msgstr ""

msgid "We also spent some time polishing our documentation as is the custom."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.14, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.15[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.15 brings support for https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-"
"accelerate-your-lambda-functions-with-lambda-snapstart/[AWS Lambda "
"SnapStart]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This has already been announced in details in https://quarkus.io/blog/"
"quarkus-support-for-aws-lambda-snapstart/[a previous blog post]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See https://quarkus.io/guides/aws-lambda-snapstart[the dedicated guide] for "
"more information about how to use AWS Lambda SnapStart with Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "New gRPC implementation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The gRPC extension has been rewritten to use a new Vert.x-based gRPC "
"implementation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Moreover `@InjectMock` is now working for gRPC Mutiny clients."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The SmallRye GraphQL extension now supports enhancing your GraphQL API with "
"metadata needed to be able to expose it via a Apollo Federation gateway.\n"
"This is achieved via annotations in the `io.smallrye.graphql.api.federation` "
"package.\n"
"See https://www.apollographql.com/docs/federation/ for general information "
"about Federation or https://smallrye.io/smallrye-graphql/2.0.0/federation/ "
"for an example."
msgstr ""

msgid "Redis - Search group"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Since the introduction of the new Redis extension, a lot of new commands "
"were added from version to version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is now commands for the search group which makes its apparition in "
"Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "<code>@ClientQueryParam</code> for Reactive REST Client"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using the Reactive REST Client, it is possible to add query parameters to a "
"request with the `@ClientQueryParam` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is described in details in https://quarkus.io/guides/rest-client-"
"reactive#using-clientqueryparam[the Reactive REST Client guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Filtering by named queries in REST Data with Panache extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Filtering by named queries has been added to the REST Data with Panache "
"extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find more information about it in https://quarkus.io/guides/rest-"
"data-panache#complex-filtering-to-list-entities-using-namedquery[the REST "
"Data with Panache guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "OIDC FrontChannel logout"
msgstr ""

msgid "The OIDC extension adds support for OIDC FrontChannel logout."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM - IN clause parameter padding enabled by default"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.15 adds the `quarkus.hibernate-orm.query.in-clause-parameter-"
"padding` configuration property to the Hibernate ORM extension,\n"
"and enables it by default."
msgstr ""

msgid "It improves the caching of queries containing IN clauses."
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid "Two major improvements for the Quarkus CLI in 2.15:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Continuous testing is available in the Quarkus CLI with the `quarkus test` "
"command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Building and pushing images is as simple as `quarkus image build` / `quarkus "
"image push`."
msgstr ""

msgid "-XX:ArchiveClassesAtExit for AppCDS creation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using Java 17+ to create AppCDS archives, Quarkus automatically enables "
"the `-XX:ArchiveClassesAtExit` option."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev Services for Kubernetes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev Services is one of the Dev Experience features that make Quarkus unique.\n"
"Quarkus 2.15 introduces Dev Services for Kubernetes so that you can easily "
"test your applications using the Kubernetes Client extension."
msgstr ""

msgid "Test framework for Google Cloud Functions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Google Cloud Functions extensions now have a test framework utility in "
"the form of the `quarkus-test-google-cloud-functions` artifact."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find more information about it in https://quarkus.io/guides/funqy-"
"gcp-functions#testing-your-function[the Google Cloud Functions guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.15.0.CR1[2.15.0.CR1] and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.15.0.Final[2.15.0.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

